"Caden's mother teaches by questions: knowing how matters more than knowing what."
"She never took up thaumaturgy, but can manifest arcana at a distance."
"When Triss choked on a fishbone she blanked on basic sequences, likely her prophecy's work."
"She and Everett scorn belief in Fateweavers, and kept Triss despite the prophecy."
"She was surprised to hear Caden speak of mind-speech without a gestalt."
"Now: Caden's mother is most likely at home in Creyvlor with Triss; Everett comes home at weekends."
"At birth Triss drew a minor prophecy to her father: 'This daughter shall be your ruin.'"
"Triss's prophecy is now subsumed into Ambrose's Major Prophecy."
"Triss has prodigious control; Caden began teaching her frameshifting last winter."
"Triss is good at using the augera's 'lines' of friendship and kinship."
"Caden's grandparents, hard-line prophecy supporters, wanted Triss given up."
"Now: Triss is most likely at home in Creyvlor with her mother, going to school."
"The Duke is strict; he barred Devon from kitchens and pushed him to become an arcanist."
"The Duke fired Governess Lane and revoked Devon's glyphic keys to the manor."
"The Duke has pull in the Empire; he had Imperial Nightwatchers set to guard his son."
"His manor was Safehouse 3 for the agents, until Sedhahn attackers struck it."
"Now: the Duke is most likely in Geldor, busy with the Empire's affairs."
"The Duchess calls Devon 'Devvy'; she lost pregnancies before he was born."
"The Duchess talked Devon out of ending his life, and once shouted down the Duke."
"The Duchess helped Devon hide the gear for his wild augera hunt."
"Now: the Duchess is most likely at the Ka'atryn home in Geldor's High District."
"The Duke dismissed Governess Lane after two weeks, paying out her week and the next month."
"Her dismissal lingers among Devon's childhood memories."
"Now: Lane's whereabouts are unknown; most likely she serves another household in Geldor."
"The twins' father caned Kevan as a boy, yet took the twins hunting big game and trekking."
"He lost his leg fighting Sedhahn agents, lives by artefacts, and grew kinder after."
"He holds a personal stake that sets the twins against the others of their dorm."
"Now: the twins' father is most likely at home in Hanafast."
"The agents belong to a secret agency working beside, but not within, the Imperial Police."
"Mr Silver heads SD-P7, Caden's detail; his Sign is Sickle, and he distrusts the Demiurge."
"Mr Silver pulled Caden from the highway ambush, sedated him, and escorted him to Geldor."
"Now: Mr Silver is most likely posted outside the Academy walls, where agents may not enter."
"Ms Rain lost her left knee in the highway ambush near Creyvlor."
"Ms Rain and Ms Fen held off superior numbers to defend Caden; Ms Fen was the driver."
"Now: Ms Rain and Ms Fen are most likely still recovering from their wounds."
"Ms Pearl heads SD-P1, Ambrose's Nightwatcher detail; her Sign is Nightshade."
"Ms Pearl alone survived a team lost to wild arcana at the border, after years abroad."
"Ms Pearl masters distortion fields without artefacts and senses non-human presences."
"Now: Ms Pearl is most likely camped outside the Academy walls, guarding Ambrose."
"Mr Garnet ran Safehouse 3 at the Ka'atryn manor and supervised the students there."
"Now: Mr Garnet is most likely still with the agency in Geldor."
"The white-haired superior commands by telepresence; agents call her ma'am."
"She refuses even her ranking agents more than they need to know."
"Now: the superior's place is unknown; most likely she directs the agency from Geldor."
"The Emperor knows the truth of the Fateweavers and is kept immune to prophetic links."
"The throne is one check on the Fateweavers, and holds only by their leave."
"Caldwell persuaded the reluctant Emperor to call arcanists into service and ready for war."
"Paval the sage speaks of a reigning Empress; whether it is Emperor or Empress is unsettled."
"Now: the sovereign is most likely in the palace at Geldor, overseeing mobilisation for war."
"The Fateweaver who met Caden is an ancient-distant-spider to the augera, once human, female."
"She is white-haired, ice-blue-eyed and grey-robed, with a maternal face that shifts in size."
"She speaks with a faintly foreign accent and shares memories with the other Fateweavers."
"She froze time, stripped Caden's augeric shell, and flung him across half the Empire."
"She wiped Caden from his friends' memories; she cannot read him without killing him."
"She wove the Dundales into the Prophecy to pose the question: is it worth it?"
"Now: her place is unknown; most likely she watches the Six and steers others around Caden."
"The Watcher is middle-aged, black-haired and emerald-eyed, and speaks through reflections."
"The Watcher says he is of neither the Empire, Sedhah, nor any nation Caden knows."
"He has befriended the augeric web, which teaches him to skulk past the Fateweavers."
"His flare cannot be sensed even up close, and he opposes the Fateweavers."
"He warned Caden about friendships, and asked if Caden had dominated any augera."
"Now: the Watcher's place is unknown since he vanished from the Academy lake."
"Atrael Ka'atus, a mighty demiurge, used glyphs to shackle the first augera."
"The first Spire was raised to hold that augera and channel its power."
"Atrael Ka'atus is most likely the same Ka'atus for whom the Ka'atus Room is named."
"Now: Atrael Ka'atus has been dead for millennia."
"Ka'atus is most likely Atrael Ka'atus, who shackled the first augera; few would guess it."
"Now: Ka'atus is long dead."
"Alyssa Nivordin treated the Spires as vast artefacts, unaware of the augera chained within."
"Her array reinforces structures, amplifies gestalts, and links to arrays in Spire foundations."
"Now: Alyssa Nivordin is long dead; her work is read in the Lower Library."
"An ancient survey in the Vault names King Felavor Erindil and Queen Merelda Laurin of the elves."
"Their realm is Cildana Gwyd, listed just below Aiesta in that survey."
"When it was written they had reigned over eighty years, guarding a secret and governing little."
"Now: whether the pair still live is unknown; the survey is very old."
